<div className={styles.pvlRoot}>
	<div class="pvlRichtext"><p><img src="https://8hxvw8tw.media.zestyio.com/IMG_4347.JPG" alt="IMG_4347.JPG"></p></div>
	<div class="pvlRichtext"><p>Thank you to everyone who attended and supported our 4th Annual Christmas in July fundraiser on July 29, 2026! We'd like to extend a special thank you to Erik Bakich, Clemson Baseball Coach, for speaking at the event, as well as our sponsors.</p>
<p><span>The event celebrates the many volunteers and community partners who participated in The Salvation Army’s Red Kettle Impact Campaign last holiday season. Their efforts helped raise $59,577, a new record set by volunteers, to support the organization’s mission programs throughout the year in Greenville. In addition, volunteers served more than 1,000 hours during the Red Kettle Season, also a new record for The Salvation Army of Greenville.</span></p>
<p><span>Christmas in July attendees had the chance to win a baseball signed by the 2025-26 Clemson Tigers Baseball Team, Luxury Box tickets to a Greenville Drive Game, and more.</span></p>
<p><span>The Salvation Army recognized the top five volunteer bell-ringing groups that raised the most funds during the Red Kettle Impact campaign. Listed alphabetically, the top volunteer groups were:</span></p>
<ul>
<li aria-level="1">
<p><span>Greenville Civitan Club</span></p>
</li>
<li aria-level="1">
<p><span>Greenville Rotary Club</span></p>
</li>
<li aria-level="1">
<p><span>Mr. &amp; Mrs. Powell's Classes, Stone Academy</span></p>
</li>
<li aria-level="1">
<p><span>The Salvation Army Women's Auxiliary</span></p>
</li>
<li aria-level="1">
<p><span>Simpsonville Rotary and Kiwanis Clubs</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span>Community partner Fox Carolina was highlighted for their generous support of The Salvation Army’s programs throughout the year. They received the Red Shield Partner Award in recognition for their support and assistance in helping hundreds of children in Greenville receive Christmas gifts through The Salvation Army’s Angel Tree program, as well as volunteering with the Red Kettle Impact Campaign.</span></p>
<p><span>Last year, The Salvation Army supported more than 44,432 unduplicated individuals in need in Greenville. Every dollar donated locally stays in Greenville to provide assistance where it's needed most.</span></p>
<p><span>The proceeds raised at the Christmas in July event:</span></p>
<ul>
<li aria-level="1">
<p><span>Provide emergency shelter to men, women, and children 365 days a year</span></p>
</li>
<li aria-level="1">
<p><span>Prepare food boxes for individuals and families experiencing food insecurity</span></p>
</li>
<li aria-level="1">
<p><span>Assist those struggling to make ends meet with utility and rent so they can stay in their homes</span></p>
</li>
<li aria-level="1">
<p><span>Coordinate disaster relief for those who have lost everything due to fire or other natural disasters</span></p>
</li>
<li aria-level="1">
<p><span>Provide spiritual and emotional care to those in need</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span>“While many people are in the giving spirit around the holidays, we serve individuals and families in need all year round,” said Major Michael Harris, Area Commander for The Salvation Army of Greenville, Pickens &amp; Oconee Counties. “We invite people to attend our Christmas in July fundraiser to help us provide critical, life-changing programs to our neighbors in Greenville struggling to make ends meet.”</span></p>
<p><span>The Salvation Army’s Christmas in July was presented by the following sponsors:</span></p>
<p><span>Gold Sponsors: Fred Collins Foundation, Shurburtt Landscaping</span></p>
<p><span>Silver Sponsors: AFL, Caldwell Constructors, First Horizon, Godshall Staffing, Millers HVAC</span></p></div>
</div>